network device. Repeated BGP authentication failures can indicate brute-force
attempts to hijack or manipulate routing — a high-impact attack that may enable
traffic interception, persistence on the routing fabric, or downstream
adversary-in-the-middle scenarios.

# Target environment
- Product: Huawei (network equipment)
- Log source service: BGP
